   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the state technology law, in relation to requiring state\nagencies to conform any of their websites to the most current version of the\nWeb Content Accessibility Guidelines adopted by the World Wide Web Consortium\nfor accessibility",
    "basePrintNo": "S8032",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8032-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Ren §103-b to be §103-d, amd §§103-d & 103, St Tech L (as proposed in S.3114-A & A.266-A)",
    "lawSection": "State Technology Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8032\n\nSPONSOR: MANNION\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the state technology law, in relation to requiring state\nagencies to conform any of their websites to the most current version of\nthe Web Content Accessibility Guidelines adopted by the World Wide Web\nConsortium for accessibility\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to the provisions of\nL.2023 c.734, to clarify compliance standards and require full compli-\nance by January 1, 2027.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by clarifying that\nwebsites must comply where there is a change to form or function. The\nchange to form or function is defined as modifications to aspects of the\nwebsite. The amendment requires all agency websites to be compliant by\nJanuary 1, 2027.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 734 of the Laws of 2023. S.3114-A and\nA.266-A both passed the Senate and Assembly, respectfully, in May 2023.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2023 state technology law, in relation to requir-\ning state agencies to conform any of their websites to the Web Content\nAccessibility Guidelines, as proposed in legislative bills numbers\nS.3114-A and A.266-A, takes effect.\n",
